<section image-layout="blank" id="debrFMFUAC"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="fhn3_82RMV" background-color="accent" padding="28pt 12pt 56pt" colspan="7"><p role="eyebrow">Field guide</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><p role="caption">GOVERNANCE</p><p role="caption">07 / 10</p></grid-item><grid-item id="AcCmfXZfCv" padding="0" colspan="53"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="kcpi1wqbWF" padding="0" colspan="8"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/nZaSdDDn_VHbXTG2OvHSg.png" saved-media-id="qwjegs8wae60xvb" source="image.ai-generated" fill="true" image-style="operational-still-life" alt="Editorial studio photograph of a strict vertical hierarchy of warm-white paper trays, an operational-blue decision tab at the top, graphite delivery cards below, one field-sage runbook band and a signal-amber escalation clip, connected by a single precise cord, soft directional daylight, no text, lettering, people, logos, or screens" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item><grid-item id="WnbBCeWxWB" padding="18pt 22pt 16pt" colspan="52"><labels><label variant="outline">Illustrative replacement · validate before use</label></labels><h2 font-size="27pt">One hierarchy of truth; clear change and escalation rules</h2><grid spacing="small" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="1-0ZCPfnHJ" colspan="25"><grid divider="sm neutral-border" marker="number" marker-position="inline" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" direction="vertical" vertical-sizing="hug" style="--marker-inline-size: 26pt; --marker-gap: 8pt;"><grid-item id="H1KxVpjeA6" padding="6pt 0"><h4 font-size="17pt">Decision log</h4><p font-size="15pt">Accepted choices, rationale, consequences, and superseded decisions.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="wJqA648nwG" padding="6pt 0"><h4 font-size="17pt">Delivery board</h4><p font-size="15pt">Active owner, status, dependency, and target sequence.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="5bs8zkMBZI" padding="6pt 0"><h4 font-size="17pt">Runbook</h4><p font-size="15pt">Launch, rollback, incident response, and routine operation.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="x-_j1Gf7W0" padding="6pt 0"><h4 font-size="17pt">Chat and meetings</h4><p font-size="15pt">Coordination only; a decision is accepted only when logged.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="q2CKArKTLc" colspan="20"><grid direction="vertical" spacing="small" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="cuIKR2hZ4S" cell-style="subtle" padding="10pt 12pt"><h4 font-size="17pt">Cadence and change control</h4><p font-size="15pt">Weekly 30-minute decision forum; delivery review twice weekly; daily asynchronous updates from T+5 through stabilization. Log changes to acceptance, data, launch sequence, or schedule shifts over two business days.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="0KC3dkiNBU" cell-style="subtle" padding="10pt 12pt"><h4 font-size="17pt">Definition of done</h4><p font-size="15pt">Done means evidence attached, runbook updated, and duty explicitly accepted by the receiving owner.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="ZXXB7k5WTt" cell-style="subtle" padding="10pt 12pt" colspan="15"><h4 font-size="17pt">Warnings and escalation</h4><p font-size="15pt">R-02 warns when refresh exceeds two hours. Escalate immediately above four hours, for queue age above five minutes, access gaps, or missing authority.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>